  "materialFindings": [
    "The actual decoded scene reads as painted stained glass within dark brown Gothic framing. A recognizable stone abbey/arched ruin is visible in a coherent woodland, sky and valley scene.",
    "Sharp frame/came and distinguishable glass/artwork remain readable at both tiers. No native-pixel contour grid, added artificial grain, invented edge bricks or abstract texture is relied upon.",
    "Upper lobes, central quatrefoil, main mullion, horizontal-bar rhythm, jambs and sill remain representative. Mid/High share the same scene and structural layout.",
    "Both exact BOX comparisons retain the pale upper glazing, dark olive/brown lower masses and principal forms at the native feature scale. Authorized painted scene interpretation changes within-pane detail; similarity rather than pixel identity is assessed."
  ],
  "lowestPaneInterpretation": {
    "nativeObservation": "The lowest native panes contain two round/radial dark-gold optical motifs; these are not claimed absent. The scene does not reproduce those exact motifs.",
    "assessment": "Native context does not unambiguously distinguish painted/optical medallions from fine leaded ornament or establish projecting solid hardware. These within-pane marks do not form the obvious heavy continuous structural connections of the mullion, arch, came and sill.",
    "decision": "The owner explicitly allowed artist-depicted stained-glass scenes. Reinterpretation of this ambiguous within-glass pattern is acceptable while retaining the actual pane/frame boundaries, distant palette and feature scale. No solid bottom rosette hardware was invented.",
    "ownerDecision": {
      "file": "docs/hexen2/textures/parallel-2026-10-20/stream-18-rtex018/owner-stained-scene-decision.json",
      "sha256": "8ef83dc86a12326cd92b689b8d047750429e90670e4033463b4b546afe104ba9"
    }
  },
  "physicalFindings": [
    "Both actual decoded height/XYZ and fixed opposed neutral/textured fields show shallow raised frame/came above flat glass. Ruin/shrine pigment and woodland imagery do not become embossed terrain.",
    "The corrected central opening retains surrounding raised continuous came. Actual coupled RGB/relief views show no renewed continuous-came invasion, frame trench, painted rim or new image-perimeter bevel.",
    "Actual Q92 data maps show finite quantization but retain the broad flat-pane/shallow-frame hierarchy. Eight height/normal maps are shared byte-identically with the qualified baseline and between variants; coupled current-scene views were still examined rather than accepting from hashes alone."
  ],
  "joinFindings": [
    "Personally reviewed both complete wrap axes, corners and2x2 RGB repeats at both tier sizes. Intentional repeated jamb/sill/frame contacts remain coherent; no unexplained extra strip, missing corner, shifted frame or carrier padding is apparent.",
    "The separately qualified mixed-pool9 ordered X/Y pairs and81 four-way corners per tier also passed actual pixel-provenance and visual review; that is scene-pool compatibility, not runtime randomization proof."
  ],
  "mixedPoolReview": {
    "file": "docs/hexen2/textures/parallel-2026-10-20/stream-18-rtex018/pool-mixed-joins-v1/independent-review-texture06-v1.json",
    "sha256": "d8e314ad345e144a56ef829c73696f93120c91020c472b3f1c0d79fe95f5ade1"
  },
